# Supabase, for asynchronous multiplayer (Phase 1).
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in from the project dashboard. `.env` is gitignored;
# this file carries the *names* and never the values.
#
# The anon key is public by design: it is compiled into the client bundle, and
# row-level security — not secrecy — is what stops one player writing to another
# player's match. Anything prefixed `VITE_` is readable by anyone who opens the
# page, so the service-role key must never appear here. That one is server-only
# and belongs in Phase 2's edge-function secrets.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
